== Stage 7 ==
;28 August 2026 – [[Vall d'Alba]] to [[Valdelinares|Aramón Valdelinares]], {{convert|149.9|km|abbr=on}}
[[Andreas Leknessund]] won stage seven, leading a Norwegian one-two ahead of [[Tobias Halland Johannessen]]. The victory came one day after the [[Death and state funeral of Harald V|death of King Harald V of Norway]], with both Norwegian riders wearing [[black armband]]s in his memory. [[Tadej Pogačar]] extended his overall lead in the general classification.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Marshall-Bell |first1=Chris |title=Vuelta a Espana stage 7: Norwegian duo seal emotional 1-2 finish on day King Harald V dies |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7546096/2026/08/28/vuelta-stage-seven-leknessund-king-harald/ |access-date=1 September 2026 |agency=The Athletic |date=28 August 2026}}</ref>
